{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request 1c001e0c, NF-2: neither. NF-2 adds no display union\nand no fixed-tool API. It leaves\npackages/cli/src/application-install-runtime.ts unchanged.\n\nWhy. NF-4 (d2aff067) scope 3 removes the `McpService` construction and\nevery `structuredContent` read from that file. The command line then\nreads a typed result from two client functions. A checked union built\nnow lives for two heads and then goes. The malformed case that it\nguards cannot occur today: the command line configures no\n`ApplicationReadCatalogue`, so only the fixed constructors answer.\n\nWhat NF-2 owes for this file.\n1. `CallResult.structuredContent` keeps the type\n   `Record\u003cstring, unknown\u003e`. It is the shape that `tools/call` sends.\n   The typed result of scope 2 serves the callers inside packages/mcp.\n2. The fixed constructors keep the members that the renderer reads:\n   `message`, `next`, `answer`, `reason`, `item`, `state`, `phase` and\n   `screen`. If the one typed result changes a name or a value among\n   them, stop and ask.\n3. The head note names this file as the one reader of\n   `structuredContent` by string key that remains in process, and it\n   names NF-4 as the head that removes it.\n\nNF-4 gives the renderer its typed input. Put the precise types on the\ntwo client functions there, and add no parser to the command line.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}